WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.520 --> 00:00:04.840
Any show with a following as massive as Stranger
Things is going to have fans throwing theories

00:00:04.860 --> 00:00:08.849
around, and over the last two seasons, viewers
have scrambled for answers to a number of

00:00:08.849 --> 00:00:09.849
questions.

00:00:09.849 --> 00:00:11.969
Some involve the mysteries of the Upside Down.

00:00:11.969 --> 00:00:13.769
Others tackle Eleven's origins.

00:00:13.769 --> 00:00:18.120
And some are just predictions of where future
seasons may take some fan favorite characters.

00:00:18.120 --> 00:00:20.380
Plenty of these ideas are just plain wacky.

00:00:20.380 --> 00:00:25.700
"However, I am on a curiosity voyage and I
need my paddles to travel."

00:00:26.250 --> 00:00:30.420
So, let's take a look at some of the Stranger
Things fan theories that may end up being

00:00:30.430 --> 00:00:31.880
accurate.

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:33.350
Daddy dearest

00:00:33.350 --> 00:00:35.320
Let's start with a fun one, shall we?

00:00:35.320 --> 00:00:39.010
Before we ventured into Hawkins, Indiana with
Stranger Things there was another small town

00:00:39.010 --> 00:00:42.309
in the Hoosier State that boasted a big-haired
beau like Steve Harrington.

00:00:42.309 --> 00:00:46.289
Parks and Recreation took place in Pawnee,
Indiana, and while that show was entirely

00:00:46.289 --> 00:00:51.219
different, its resident silly man Jean-Ralphio
looks an awful lot like Steve, which has led

00:00:51.219 --> 00:00:54.289
some theorists to believe that they may be
father and son.

00:00:54.289 --> 00:00:58.300
Since Parks and Rec takes place in the modern
era, and Stranger Things is set in the '80s,

00:00:58.300 --> 00:01:02.160
the timelines match up just as well as their
hairstyles, so it's definitely a workable

00:01:02.160 --> 00:01:03.160
fan theory.

00:01:03.160 --> 00:01:06.740
And the actors portraying the characters have
since played along with the popular notion

00:01:06.740 --> 00:01:07.740
as well.

00:01:07.740 --> 00:01:08.740
"You're my father.

00:01:08.740 --> 00:01:09.740
You're my father."

00:01:09.740 --> 00:01:10.740
"What did you just say?"

00:01:10.740 --> 00:01:14.850
The only question is, who's gonna be the lucky
Mrs. Harrington with whom he has young Jean-Ralphio?

00:01:14.850 --> 00:01:17.630
And speaking of paternity theories...

00:01:17.630 --> 00:01:18.810
Hopper's daughter

00:01:18.810 --> 00:01:22.250
The first season explains that Chief Hopper's
young daughter died years before the show

00:01:22.250 --> 00:01:26.189
began, but some have suggested that her death
might have ultimately been a cover-up for

00:01:26.189 --> 00:01:27.469
her abduction.

00:01:27.469 --> 00:01:30.729
The people behind the Hawkins Lab already
proved they could fake a death with Will in

00:01:30.729 --> 00:01:34.189
Season 1, and we now have confirmation that
the children they put through the program

00:01:34.189 --> 00:01:35.630
are abductees.

00:01:35.630 --> 00:01:40.159
It seems totally possible that Hopper's daughter
was one of their experiments—perhaps Number

00:01:40.159 --> 00:01:42.289
1 to 7, 9, or 10.

00:01:42.289 --> 00:01:46.579
On the other hand, there are also some who
believe Eleven might actually be his daughter.

00:01:46.579 --> 00:01:50.430
Sure, she's able to sniff out files that make
her believe she's Jane, the long-lost daughter

00:01:50.430 --> 00:01:54.259
of another telekinetic woman whose daughter
was stolen, but Hopper's the one who had those

00:01:54.259 --> 00:01:55.520
files hidden in his house.

00:01:55.520 --> 00:01:59.420
Wouldn't it be something if the reason he
was transferring so much protective fatherly

00:01:59.420 --> 00:02:03.490
energy to Eleven is that she actually is his
own flesh and blood?

00:02:03.490 --> 00:02:05.130
Stranger things have happened.

00:02:05.130 --> 00:02:06.130
Career path

00:02:06.130 --> 00:02:09.409
There's no doubt that Steve was the surprise
MVP of Season 2.

00:02:09.409 --> 00:02:13.870
But what's next for the former pretty-boy
bully remains to be seen, as his entire post-graduation

00:02:13.870 --> 00:02:17.260
plan seemed to revolve around Nancy, who he's
no longer with.

00:02:17.260 --> 00:02:21.000
He spent the whole season subbing in as a
big brother slash babysitter for Dustin and

00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:26.040
the other kids, so now some are drawing parallel
lines between his arc and that of Chief Hopper.

00:02:26.040 --> 00:02:29.840
Considering the fact that Hopper has no one
he can trust with all this sensitive information

00:02:29.840 --> 00:02:34.160
about the other side on his own squad, perhaps
he'll recruit Steve to join the force and

00:02:34.160 --> 00:02:35.250
become his new deputy.

00:02:35.250 --> 00:02:39.400
The only real question is whether he'd be
allowed to maintain his signature mane while

00:02:39.400 --> 00:02:40.400
in uniform.

00:02:41.660 --> 00:02:43.640
"We're in such deep s---."

00:02:43.640 --> 00:02:44.640
The upside-down

00:02:44.640 --> 00:02:49.060
As far as we know, the upside-down is a parallel
dimension that was accidentally opened by

00:02:49.060 --> 00:02:53.630
all those government experiments gone wrong,
and now that Eleven's worked her supreme magic,

00:02:53.630 --> 00:02:54.659
the gate is closed.

00:02:54.659 --> 00:02:56.989
But what if there's more to it than that?

00:02:56.989 --> 00:03:00.349
We know from the last shot that the fight
against the mind flayer is far from done,

00:03:00.349 --> 00:03:04.659
but what if instead of fighting a parallel
world, this is a battle against the future?

00:03:04.659 --> 00:03:08.879
The Upside Down is characterized by images
of a Hawkins ravaged by destruction, decay,

00:03:08.879 --> 00:03:09.879
and rot.

00:03:09.879 --> 00:03:13.260
Perhaps instead of seeing some second dimension,
what's trickling into the scene is a dreadful

00:03:13.260 --> 00:03:16.019
sense of inevitability that's itching to come
true now.

00:03:16.019 --> 00:03:19.950
The mind flayer may be some Terminator-style
time traveler who's ready to take over the

00:03:19.950 --> 00:03:24.040
town, and possibly the world, sooner rather
than later.

00:03:24.040 --> 00:03:25.200
New spies

00:03:25.200 --> 00:03:29.780
Season 2 of Stranger Things sees the show's
new big bad, the Mind Flayer, possess Will

00:03:29.780 --> 00:03:31.540
Byers and turn him into his spy.

00:03:31.540 --> 00:03:35.360
We still know very little about this monster,
but his possession of Will at least gave us

00:03:35.360 --> 00:03:37.780
a few answers as to how he functions.

00:03:37.780 --> 00:03:42.000
The most important tidbit: contact with him
can have lingering effects, namely in regards

00:03:42.000 --> 00:03:45.180
to his ability to spy on our world through
those he's touched.

00:03:45.180 --> 00:03:49.250
Given this, a few fans seem to think that
he's already found his next set of eyes.

00:03:49.250 --> 00:03:53.200
While exploring the tunnels beneath Hawkins,
both Hopper and Dustin discover a weird object

00:03:53.200 --> 00:03:55.720
on the wall that shoots a strange substance
onto them.

00:03:55.720 --> 00:03:59.590
They clean it off in short order and little
is said of it past that, but the Duffer Brothers

00:03:59.590 --> 00:04:02.959
aren't the kind of showrunners to introduce
something like that if it isn't going to pay

00:04:02.959 --> 00:04:03.969
off later.

00:04:03.969 --> 00:04:07.879
This has led many to believe that Dustin and
Hopper are now infected by the Mind Flayer

00:04:07.879 --> 00:04:10.989
and will perhaps act as his new spies.

00:04:10.989 --> 00:04:11.989
Fast forward

00:04:11.989 --> 00:04:15.810
The time jump between seasons 1 and 2 of Stranger
Things was roughly one year.

00:04:15.810 --> 00:04:20.109
But many fans posit that the show will jump
forward even further in future seasons.

00:04:20.109 --> 00:04:23.810
Considering how quickly the child stars are
aging, it might not be too unreasonable to

00:04:23.810 --> 00:04:27.639
expect the series to bypass the one year mark
and take them straight into high school in

00:04:27.639 --> 00:04:28.639
Season 3.

00:04:28.639 --> 00:04:32.300
If so, that'd put the show near the tail end
of the decade and open up a whole new strain

00:04:32.300 --> 00:04:34.370
of cinematic callback potential.

00:04:34.370 --> 00:04:36.580
Think The Fly and Terminator and The Lost
Boys.

00:04:36.580 --> 00:04:40.220
If they wait long enough to launch production
on a third season, they could very well hop

00:04:40.220 --> 00:04:44.651
into the next decade -- the '90s -- and start
throwing out homages to sci-fi pics of that

00:04:44.651 --> 00:04:47.410
era like The Abyss and Tremors and Jurassic
Park.

00:04:47.410 --> 00:04:48.720
It could happen.

00:04:48.720 --> 00:04:50.360
Spin off

00:04:50.360 --> 00:04:53.970
The seventh episode of Stranger Things 2 has
left a lot of viewers divided over whether

00:04:53.970 --> 00:04:58.360
Eleven really even needed to venture out to
Chicago to link up with her lost institution

00:04:58.360 --> 00:05:01.310
sister Kali, who also bears the number eight
on her wrist.

00:05:01.310 --> 00:05:04.430
But while Eleven was figuring out that her
friends in Hawkins were important enough to

00:05:04.430 --> 00:05:08.270
fight for, there's still a story to be told
through Kali's mission for vengeance.

00:05:08.270 --> 00:05:12.340
Sure, her appearance could just be a preview
of clutch reunions to come for all the lab's

00:05:12.340 --> 00:05:15.920
other missing children, but it could also
be the first attempt to spark a spin-off for

00:05:15.920 --> 00:05:16.920
the series.

00:05:16.920 --> 00:05:21.560
The unpopularity of the episode might derail
any plans for producing a Kali-centric spin-off,

00:05:21.560 --> 00:05:25.270
but don't be surprised if the Duffer Brothers
give it another shot with some more new characters

00:05:25.270 --> 00:05:26.509
in the coming seasons.

00:05:26.509 --> 00:05:27.710
Thanks for watching!

00:05:27.710 --> 00:05:30.110
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:05:30.110 --> 00:05:32.330
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

